# Generated outputs. The model regenerates all of these from the YAML in one
# command, so they are build artefacts, not source. The exception is
# validation/baselines/*.json, which IS committed -- see below.
dist/
export_output/
*.xlsx
*.xls
*.pdf
*.csv

# The explorer's data bundle is generated from the model. The page is source;
# its data is not.
explorer/data.json

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Editors and OS
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Temporary Excel lock files, in case the source workbook is open nearby
~$*

# NOT ignored, deliberately:
#
#   validation/baselines/*.json  -- the frozen figures Excel itself produced.
#   Committing them means the port can be re-validated on a machine with no
#   Excel installed, and that any change to the reference numbers shows up as
#   a reviewable diff rather than a silent shift.
!validation/baselines/*.json
#
#   reference/*.xlsx  -- the original workbook the model was ported from.
#   The *.xlsx rule above exists to keep generated exports out of the repo;
#   this one file is not an export, it is the source. See reference/README.md.
!reference/*.xlsx
#
#   assumptions/*.csv  -- the Tontine liability run-off curve exported from the
#   actuarial model. The *.csv rule above is aimed at generated data dumps in
#   dist/; this one is INPUT the engine cannot run without. It was silently
#   swallowed once and CI caught it, which is the second time a broad
#   extension rule has eaten a source file here. Anything under assumptions/
#   is input by definition.
!assumptions/*.csv
